// pfodWeb NOTE: dedicated-hardware pin-exclusion audit (2026-07-12). This
// is the real "PowerFeather ESP32-S3" (Feather-format, LiFePO4/Li-ion/LiPo
// solar power-management board, USB_MANUFACTURER "PowerFeather"). Sources
// consulted: official docs source
// https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PowerFeather/powerfeather-docs/main/docs/hardware/esp32s3.md
// ("Pins & Signals" tables: User-Managed Fixed IO / Free IO / SDK-Managed
// Fixed IO / Special Function) and the vendor Arduino/IDF SDK source
// https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PowerFeather/powerfeather-sdk/main/src/Mainboard/Mainboard.h
// (authoritative `Pin` struct, lines ~109-114) plus Mainboard.cpp (confirms
// `_i2cPort = 1` = Wire1 dedicated to onboard PMIC comms). Findings per
// flagged pin:
//   - GPIO21 (ALARM) - Mainboard.h: `ALARM = GPIO_NUM_21; // Battery fuel
//     gauge alarm`. Docs: "Battery Fuel Gauge Alarm Input", and
//     Mainboard.h's alarm-setter comments state "the ALARM pin is pulled
//     low" by the onboard fuel gauge IC (LC709204F on V1 / MAX17260 on
//     V2). Dedicated PMIC alarm line - EXCLUDED. High confidence.
//   - GPIO5 (INT) - Mainboard.h: `INT = GPIO_NUM_5; // Battery charge
//     interrupt`. Docs: "Battery Charger Interrupt Input" from the onboard
//     charger IC (BQ25628E on V2). Dedicated PMIC interrupt line -
//     EXCLUDED. High confidence.
//   - GPIO7 (EN) - Mainboard.h: `EN = GPIO_NUM_7; // FeatherWings
//     enable/disable (read)`. Docs list it under "Special Function":
//     "Feather Wing Enable Output" - used by user code to detect/emulate
//     the Feather-standard EN pin behavior (disabling `3V3`/`VSQT` load
//     switches, entering deep-sleep) rather than as a free digital I/O.
//     Dedicated board-power-control line - EXCLUDED. High confidence.
//   - GPIO46 (LED) - Mainboard.h: `LED = GPIO_NUM_46; // User LED`. Docs:
//     "Green User LED Output", RTCIO7. Confirmed dedicated onboard status
//     LED - KEPT. Polarity (active-high vs active-low drive) is NOT
//     stated in the docs source, the SDK header/source (no LED gpio_set_
//     level call - the SDK never drives this pin, it's left for user
//     sketch code), the demo repo (github.com/PowerFeather/powerfeather-
//     demo - no LED usage), or the ESPHome external component. Per this
//     repo's policy (see e.g. esp8266/wifiduino GPIO2), left WITHOUT a
//     led_high/led_low tag rather than guessing - capabilities unchanged
//     from chip-level default, single explanatory note added.
//   - GPIO0 (BTN) - Mainboard.h: `BTN = GPIO_NUM_0; // User button`.
//     Docs: "User Button Input", RTCIO0. Confirmed onboard user button -
//     KEPT, tagged with the restricted ["digital_input","button"] set
//     (matching this repo's convention, e.g. esp32c6-evb GPIO9), dropping
//     digital_output/pwm_output since it's a dedicated button input line.
//     GPIO0's existing chip-level strapping pinNote ("Must be HIGH for
//     normal boot") is unrelated/unchanged.
//   - GPIO43 (TX0) - Docs explicitly place TX0 in the "Free IO" table
//     (not User-Managed or SDK-Managed Fixed IO): "IO signals not
//     connected to anything on-board; user code is free to configure and
//     use these for any purpose". It is a genuinely distinct physical pin
//     from this board's TX=GPIO44/RX=GPIO42 (not an alias of them) - it
//     happens to be the ESP32-S3's default hardware UART0 pin, used only
//     as the SDK's default boot/log console, but the vendor explicitly
//     documents it as user-repurposable. KEPT unchanged (chip-level
//     default capabilities already cover it) - no exclusion warranted.
//   - GPIO48 (SCL1) / GPIO47 (SDA1) - Docs place these under "SDK-Managed
//     Fixed IO": "STEMMA QT I2C SCL"/"SDA", explicitly warning "User code
//     should not configure and use these IO, as doing so can cause faulty
//     behavior." Mainboard.cpp confirms this is `Wire1` (`_i2cPort = 1`),
//     used internally by the SDK to talk to the onboard fuel gauge and
//     charger ICs (shared with the physical STEMMA QT connector). This
//     matches this repo's precedent for a dedicated internal-PMIC/sensor
//     I2C bus (Nebula_S3's SDA1/SCL1 IMU-bus exclusion; Alfredo-NoU3's
//     Wire1 IMU-bus exclusion) - EXCLUDED. Medium-high confidence (vendor
//     explicitly warns against direct use, even though the connector is
//     physically STEMMA-QT-shaped).
// Alias-collision check (per playbook): none of ALARM(21)/INT(5)/EN(7)/
// LED(46)/BTN(0)/SCL1(48)/SDA1(47) collide with this board's primary-bus
// aliases SS(-1,invalid)/MOSI(40)/MISO(41)/SCK(39)/SCL(36)/SDA(35)/
// TX(44)/RX(42) - no build_boards.js bus-capability contamination risk.
// pins_arduino.h was edited to delete the `ALARM`, `INT`, `EN`, `SCL1`/
// `SDA1` (+ `WIRE1_PIN_DEFINED`) static const aliases for the excluded
// GPIOs, per the parser-union gotcha (an alias left in place re-adds the
// GPIO to the generated pin list even with the chipGpios entry removed).
// See boardsDetails/esp32/esp32s3/esp32s3_powerfeather/notes.txt for the
// full source list and per-pin reasoning.
{
